","position":{"commit_sha":"bad0ec87db1e4f0222b86cedcb4af79e3c222e27","position":"1787041068522810001-ccb42e13-e7af-46a8-be0e-9288dc7306b9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f310ca225121350fcbca232167d5577faeca7c6de22a632a12aebcd544b4b298","event_uuid":"064cd9b9-8178-44ef-a0af-616dd72fb8d4","position":{"commit_sha":"fe474fe1ec5c0497b6d6ae676df4b75c5b0d42e5","position":"1787041408410134001-064cd9b9-8178-44ef-a0af-616dd72fb8d4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"574dd4126eb81f9178456441b456543ba80f3a86dd4efac87b509466f75dbe72","event_uuid":"5f79e35d-84d9-4973-ac22-f65186e80e05","position":{"commit_sha":"38c962fc8cc590cf324202a6b348dd33d83c7ac6","position":"1787041668432039001-5f79e35d-84d9-4973-ac22-f65186e80e05"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed root cause: all seven listed fixtures copy the complete insertion-ordered `os.environ` into a subprocess mapping and return that mapping directly or nested in a rendered box. On an unrelated assertion failure, pytest default long traceback renders the fixture/test argument with `saferepr`, so arbitrary inherited values early enough in the mapping enter test output. Changeable sites: materialize_probe.py:91, fetch_secrets.py:102, disk_pressure.py:107, health_gate.py:118, signals_gerrit_config.py:87, observability_exit.py:68, and interfaces/facades/test_cli.py:46. Runtime discriminant: with `SIBLING_TRACE_SECRET=TOP_SECRET_XIPHO` inserted first, an in-memory plugin forced an unrelated failure only after each real shipped test returned. All five autodeploy surfaces plus observability produced long traceback rc=1 with sentinel count=1, while the same tests under `--tb=short` produced rc=1 with sentinel count=0. For CLI, `_cli` was replaced in-memory so no child ran; long still rendered `offline_acli_env` with the sentinel and short did not. This rules out bash/CLI stdout or stderr as the carrier. A complete 24-test run under `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` passed, rejecting any behavioral requirement for arbitrary ambient inheritance. Required allowlists are: fake-bin-first PATH plus STATE_DIR/DEPLOY_REPO/COMPOSE_DIR/MIRROR_DIR for materialize/fetch/signals/disk; the same plus HEALTH_TIMEOUT=1 for health; PATH plus six explicit offset/log paths for observability; PATH only for CLI, with REBAR_ROOT added by its consumer and Jira credentials absent by construction. Per-case mappings remain mutable. Historical blame shows seven independent feature commits, proving a repeated harness construct rather than one regression commit. Legitimacy: defect, anchored by the landed parent contract `test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py` and commit 034e17209c, plus this ticket AC. Caller sweep found only the cited subprocess/helpers; none enumerates or depends on arbitrary keys, and the minimal-env run is dynamic proof all callers are incidental. Expected repair is an allowlisted mutable mapping preserving fake PATH and explicit overrides while omitting unrelated ambient values.","timestamp":1787032074993125001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Problem: seven real pytest fixtures returned complete copies of os.environ and exposed arbitrary ambient secrets when failures rendered fixture arguments/locals.\n\nProven root cause: dict(os.environ) at the seven recorded fixture seams copied unrelated caller credentials into values pytest serializes. Runtime proof inserted a first-position synthetic sentinel; long traceback/local rendering leaked it exactly once on every fixture, while short traceback did not and replacing child invocation did not affect the CLI leak. Minimal PATH-only environments passed all affected behavior tests, ruling out dependency on arbitrary ambient keys.\n\nTest: held-out tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py was RED on all seven real fixture surfaces, GREEN after a blind fix, and the exact dict(os.environ) mutation at offline_acli_env returned its case to RED. The child harness now carries only the synthetic sentinel and PATH.\n\nFix: each fixture now returns a fresh mutable allowlisted mapping containing only its required PATH/state/path settings; health retains HEALTH_TIMEOUT=1, observability retains its offsets and REPL_LOG, and CLI remains fake-acli-first with Jira credentials absent by construction.\n\nScope & safety: all mappings remain mutable for existing overrides; no production code or dependency changed and no test was weakened. Focused result: 42 passed, 1 integration deselected after the parallel-gate .mypy_cache interference was rerun sequentially. make lint and make typecheck passed.\n\nSiblings: the seven guaranteed fixture-argument surfaces were fixed. The distinct class of 103 test-local subprocess mappings is tracked in antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch; production/maintenance propagation sites are accepted exclusions because preserving caller configuration is their product contract.\n\nReplication: the original long-trace sentinel leak no longer reproduces on any of the seven surfaces; all fourteen long/short oracle cases pass.","timestamp":1787033351832270001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-attested gate evidence, recorded by RebarBotNava at 2026-08-18T08:17:25Z against merged Gerrit change 1851 / aa41c2e45ad10da6296f6b642d0eed9e9ba76d6e: ran env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-debug-sibling-env/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q over the seven affected fixture modules plus tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py; result 42 passed, 1 skipped in 30.37s (exit 0). This subsumes the focused suite and revalidates behavior under a minimal parent environment. Gerrit Verified run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32111971923 completed SUCCESS on the merged patchset and includes gating lint, mypy typecheck, and the full Linux/macOS test matrices. The earlier 24-test minimal-parent subset is therefore covered by the stricter 42-pass rerun above.","timestamp":1787041068522810001}],"created_at":1787022382255242001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ea1f0fbf-c7f1-4f5f-8456-c8d42795ca01","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5192-f8c9-4385-4998"}],"description":"## Context\nThe RCA for broadish-permanent-condor found seven additional `@pytest.fixture` functions that return a full `dict(os.environ)` directly or nested inside the fixture argument pytest renders. Default long tracebacks can print early ambient credentials through `saferepr`. Confirmed fixtures: `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py`, `test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py`, `test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`, `test_autodeploy_health_gate.py`, `test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`, `test_observability_exit.py`, and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py`.\n\nThe scope boundary is the decorated pytest-fixture return path. An AST sweep found no eighth fixture. In particular, `test_autodeploy_materialize_certbot.py::_make_box` is a plain helper whose result is assigned to a test local, so an unrelated later assertion does not render it as a fixture argument; a runtime long/short traceback probe confirmed the sentinel stays absent. A distinct exception-time carrier exists for 103 test-local subprocess mappings when the subprocess call itself raises; follow-up `antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch` owns that larger audit. Runtime/maintenance environment propagation is excluded because preserving caller credentials/config is a separate product contract.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a parametrized real-pytest RED oracle using insertion-ordered synthetic sentinels and deterministic unrelated failures for each of the seven decorated fixture surfaces.\n- Replace each broad ambient copy with an explicit mutable allowlist: fake-bin-first `PATH` plus that harness's declared variables and per-test overrides. This is preferred over a representation wrapper because the subprocess contract itself should be explicit, the 24-test minimal-parent-environment run proves arbitrary keys are unnecessary, and it avoids adding a shared abstraction solely for test fixtures.\n- Prove sentinel absence under default long traceback and preserve the short-traceback negative control.\n- Run every existing fixture consumer under the minimal parent environment and the normal focused suites.\n- Reintroduce the exact broad-copy mutation and require the oracle to return to RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Each of the seven decorated fixtures has a deterministic RED failure-rendering probe.\n- [x] No decorated fixture in the AST construct sweep returns arbitrary ambient values.\n- [x] Default long traceback output contains no synthetic ambient sentinel on any of the seven surfaces.\n- [x] The fake-bin-first `PATH` remains available to every existing fixture consumer.\n- [x] Explicit harness environment variables remain mutable by their existing tests.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The 24-test minimal-parent-environment suite passes.\n  provenance: environment=minimal-parent-worktree-aa41c2e45a; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — 42-pass real pytest fixture/subprocess run under env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin\n- [x] [operator-attested] Focused suites pass.\n  provenance: environment=minimal-parent-worktree-aa41c2e45a; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — affected real fixture consumers plus held-out rendering oracle\n- [x] [operator-attested] Lint passes.\n  provenance: environment=gerrit-ci-run-32111971923; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — canonical gating Ruff, formatting, and repository policy checks\n- [x] [operator-attested] Typecheck passes.\n  provenance: environment=gerrit-ci-run-32111971923; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — canonical gating mypy run\n- [x] The exact broad-copy mutation returns the security oracle to RED.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_health_gate.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py","reason":"replace broad ambient fixture environment with explicit allowlist"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test